    "updated_at": "2026-11-23T21:01:06Z",
    "body": "Clarification from the maintainer (chat, 2026-11-23). His words: \"we are not REMOVING the other lead in strategies, we should give warnings if they are picked instead of the ones that should be used.\"\n\nWhat this changes:\n- Helix, Ramp and Plunge stay as lead-in types. Do not remove them from the code, the project file, the UI or MCP.\n- On a pass with \"Pass starts at\" = Inside or Outside, the default lead-in is the entry in air with an arc in the cut plane (#3746).\n- If the user selects Helix, Ramp or Plunge for such a pass, the operation uses the user's choice. It also gives a warning on the operation and in the status line. The warning names the selected type and the recommended type, and gives the reason in one plain sentence.\n- Only the automatic entries that the user did not select are removed: the dead-end ramp that PR #3577 added, and each fallback that changes the selected Arc entry into a helix, a ramp or an axial dive without a warning.\n- If the selected entry is not possible, the operation does not fall back silently. It refuses the entry with a diagnostic, or it uses a safe entry and names it in a warning (Prime Directive).\n\nPins:\n1. A pass with a user-selected Helix, Ramp or Plunge keeps that entry and has exactly one warning that names it.\n2. A pass with Arc (the default) has no helix or ramp move and no warning.\n3. No automatic ramp or helix appears that the user did not select.\n\nThe Lead in / Lead out page: do not grey out Helix, Ramp and Plunge for Inside or Outside. Show the warning text next to the selector when one of them is selected. See #3746 for the page check.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
